0 PointWeaver — two-motor five-bar path tracer
0 Name: pointweaver.ldr
0 Author: CrispStrobe
0 !LDRAW_ORG Unofficial_Model
0 !LICENSE Redistributable under the BSD-3-Clause license; see ../LICENSE.
0 // Original mechanism, frame, program and lessons by CrispStrobe.
0 // One SPIKE hub; left angular motor on port A and right angular motor on port B.
0 // Planar five-bar: fixed pivots L=(-100,0), R=(100,0) LDU in world X/Z.
0 // Link spans: input arms 80 LDU; forearms 160 LDU. All joint axes are parallel to +Y.
0 // Saved encoder datum A=0, B=0 places endpoint P=(-35,175) LDU.
0 // Program corner route: lower-left -> lower-right -> upper-right -> upper-left -> lower-left.
0 // Qualified analytical/manual encoder bounds: A=-2..34 degrees; B=-26..11 degrees.
0 // Software bounds are not physical stops. Native runtime, collisions and hardware remain UNTESTED.
0 // Measure endpoint at endpoint_marker local origin relative to base_cross_-40 local origin.
0 // External standard LDraw meshes are referenced, not embedded. Connect motors to hub ports A/B.
